==============================================================================
PART 1 -- exact symbolic assembly (R(z) kept exact via sigma(z))
==============================================================================
1+c(z) [with R(z)=(1-sigma)/z] = (eps*sigma*z - sigma + 1)/(eps*z)
coeff(KB)     = -(-eps**2*sigma*z + eps*sigma*z**2 + eps*sigma - eps - sigma*z)/(eps**2*z)
coeff(F2-F1)  = -sigma*(eps*z - 1)/eps

==============================================================================
PART 2 -- rigorous O(1/z^2) bound on coeff(F2-F1) - (-1/z)
==============================================================================
coeff(F2-F1)-(-1/z) - [(1-sigma*z^2)/z + sigma/eps] = 0  (must be 0)
CONFIRMED: coeff(F2-F1) - (-1/z) = (1-sigma*z^2)/z + sigma/eps

From s01b (Gordon bracket, exact, non-asymptotic):
  1/(1+z^2) <= 1-z^2*sigma(z) <= 3/(z^2+3)      for all z>0
  0 <= sigma(z) <= 1/(1+z^2)  <= 1/z^2                        (s01 G2)

=> |(1-sigma*z^2)/z| <= 3/(z(z^2+3)) = O(1/z^3)
=> |sigma/eps|        <= 1/(eps*(1+z^2)) = O(1/(eps*z^2))
=> |coeff(F2-F1)-(-1/z)| <= 3/(z(z^2+3)) + 1/(eps*(1+z^2))
   = O(1/(eps*z^2))   [RIGOROUS, uses ONLY R(z)'s own properties --
     NO Lipschitz/C^1 regularity of f needed for this piece.]

